WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
Good morning Hank,
it’s Tuesday. So three

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.160
and a half years ago,
I was diagnosed with a disease

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.400
called labyrinthitis, wherein part
of my inner ear became inflamed

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.200
due to a viral infection.
All at once, I went from

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.080
feeling like I had a bit of a
head cold to being completely

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.920
incapacitated by vertigo.
I fell over, began vomiting and

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:21.280
was rushed to the hospital.
In the years since, I’ve had

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.200
a lot of treatment for labyrinthitis,
and I’ve started to wonder:

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.600
Is this disease mental
or physical?

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.400
Let me just begin by noting
how profoundly we stigmatize

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.040
mental illness: When I was in
the hospital, there was initially

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.520
some thought that my vertigo
might be psychosomatic--

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.480
that the dizziness could be caused
by my chronic anxiety.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.800
And I have to confess that
once they found an ostensibly

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:44.960
physiological cause for my vertigo--
I was a little relieved because

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:48.720
suddenly everyone was acting
as if--and I started feeling as

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.400
if--my illness was really real.
But of course, mental illness

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.240
is also really real, and often
has a physiological cause.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:59.040
Like, the brains of many
people who have OCD,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:02.960
as I do, look different in
fmri scans than the brains

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.840
of other people. We just
don’t really understand those

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.720
differences very well yet. And
illnesses that are poorly

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.840
understood or lack effective
treatments tend to be heavily

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.960
stigmatized--see also,
endometriosis and irritable

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:17.840
bowel syndrome and many
pain disorders and leprosy.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.880
Rarely do I need a footnote
in a video, but I do need one here.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.400
The category of mental illness
is just that: a category.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.760
It has uses, and it has
limitations, and remembering

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:30.960
that categories are often
useful but almost always

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.000
limited seems to me one
of the big challenges of life

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.720
right now. Like, the extremely
silly discourse about whether

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.760
a hot dog is a sandwich is of
course very silly, but underneath

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:43.440
it lies something important,
which is that we want categories

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.280
to be strict and inviolable,
when in fact they are messy

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.000
and constructed.
But right, so I got labyrinthitis,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:52.880
which is not a psychological
illness, or at least I’m told

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.680
it’s not. I went home from the
hospital with two medications:

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.320
One is a central nervous
depressant called meclizine,

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:01.600
and the other an anti-anxiety
medication called Diazepam

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:04.640
that also lessens vertigo. Both
these medications were

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:07.120
psychotropic in the sense
that they affected the way

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.080
I experience consciousness,
and both of them are sometimes

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:13.520
prescribed as psychiatric
medications, but in my case

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.800
they weren’t psychiatric
medicines, because in my case

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.760
my illness was not
considered psychiatric.

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:22.320
Both these medications reduced
my symptoms while I recovered,

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:24.720
but I eventually found that even
after I was mostly better

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:27.600
and the virus was gone,
I still had some long term

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.480
problems with my vestibular
system, so my doctor sent me

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:32.720
for therapy at a
Balance Institute.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:35.360
So I went to this place to
retrain my brain’s balance system,

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.680
and while I was there the
therapist said to me,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:40.640
“We’re just trying to
rewire your brain,” and in that

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:45.200
moment I realized, this is just
like that other therapy I go to.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.440
In regular therapy, I am trying
to get my brain to respond

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.640
differently to unreliable anxious
thoughts, and in this therapy

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.080
I am trying to get my brain to
respond differently to unreliable

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:56.320
inner ear information.
Now the exercises and

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.560
medicines used to treat
OCD are very different

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.120
from those to treat labyrinthitis,
but the underlying

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.280
idea is similar. Medication
and therapy. And so is it a

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.400
mental or physical illness?
Yeah. Yes, it is.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:13.600
I find myself going back again
and again to Elaine Scarry’s

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:17.840
observation in The Body in Pain:
To have great pain is to have

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.320
certainty; to hear that another
person has pain is to have doubt.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.280
I think that doubt compounds
the suffering of people in pain,

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.640
and I think it is further compounded
when we imagine that someone’s

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:34.080
pain is less real because it involves
the mind, or because an observer

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.360
can’t see it. The truth is, the
body/mind dichotomy is as

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:40.960
insufficient as the category
of sandwiches. Our minds

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:44.480
are made out of body,
and our bodies think--in fact,

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:48.080
on Earth at least, bodies
are the only things that think.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.880
Whether we call it mental or
physical, other people’s

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.520
pain is as real as our own.
Hank, I’ll see you on Friday.

